# Tauri commands

- Command names are `snake_case`. Register each one in `generate_handler!` in `src-tauri/src/lib.rs`.
- Structs that cross the bridge use `#[serde(rename_all = "camelCase")]`.
- Return `Result<T, String>`.
- Git and other blocking work uses `spawn_blocking` or the `spawn_git` helper in `lib.rs`. Synchronous commands run on the webview thread.
- Shell out to system `git`. Do not vendor a git implementation or store credentials in the app.

```rust
#[tauri::command]
async fn repo_diff(path: String) -> Result<RepoDiff, String> {
    spawn_git(move || read_repo_diff(Path::new(&path))).await?
}
```
